I marked the invalid cases as unlikely and split the null check from the bounds check so the valid path remains fall-through and the cold returns are out of line. This reduces branch/layout overhead in the hot decode path while preserving behavior.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(profile == NULL, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;

    if (__builtin_expect(profileIndex >= profile->numFields, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;

    return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```